RF.put("questb:b40",{"8520":{"id":8520,"t":"The Alliance Needs Silk Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 43.","obj":"Bring 20 Silk Bandages to Nurse Stonefield at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Silk Bandage","desc":"With the Ahn'Qiraj War looming we need to do everything that we can to see to it that our soldiers have everything that they need. We're doing just that right here. For my part I've been placed in charge of seeing to it that we collect enough silk bandages.\nDo you think you can help me out, ‹class›?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"I need those tunics and headbands made, and I also need that piece of wildvine before I will share with you the knowledge of Wild Leather helmets.\nHead gear is highly coveted amongst adventurers, whether it be a disarmingly simple headband or a full-covering helmet. The fundamentals of creating valued head gear remain constant, no matter what the cosmetic appearance of the gear is.","done":"This Nightscape equipment you have supplied fills the order perfectly, ‹name›. I expect no less from a leatherworker of your caliber.\nYou have definitely earned this pattern. I give it to you freely, and hope you will profit from it accordingly.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.9,"y":33.6,"n":"Nurse Stonefield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8600":{"id":8600,"t":"The Horde Needs Rugged Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 55.","obj":"Bring 10 Rugged Leather to Doctor Serratus at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n10 Rugged Leather sold by Lhara","desc":"I find that the fit of the knife in your palm is more important than the edge on it. Even the dullest blade can be made to cut if pressure is being properly applied through it, wouldn't you agree, ‹class›? But you and I don't have such problems as we maintain the sharpest of edges, yes?\nWell, no matter, I have a task for you. In service to the Horde, and to do your part for the Ahn'Qiraj war effort, I want you to return to me with a number of rugged leather skins. This is something that you will do, no?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"It couldn't possibly be taking you this long to slice off ten rugged leather for me! Perhaps you should sharpen your skinning knife? Or, perhaps I am mistaken and you have them there in your pack?","done":"Very well, it appears you've done a fairly decent job of it, though some of those skins look a bit ragged about the edges. No matter, the task is completed, and you have earned your reward. Should you come across another stack of rugged leather, be sure to bring them to me posthaste.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.2,"y":72.5,"n":"Doctor Serratus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8440":{"id":8440,"t":"Conquering Arathi Basin","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.\nThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 1,500\n+50 reputation with The Defilers","back":"You've come back with news from Arathi, ‹class›?","done":"Securing our resources in Arathi is an important task! You've done well, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8120":{"id":8120,"t":"The Battle for Arathi Basin!","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Assault the Arathi Basin mine, lumber mill, blacksmith and stable, and then return to Deathmaster Dwire in Hammerfall.\nMine Assaulted\nLumber Mill Assaulted\nBlacksmith Assaulted\nStable Assaulted","desc":"As you no doubt have heard, the League of Arathor is sending large numbers of troops into Arathi Basin. Eager for food and supplies, these Alliance fools are intent to take and control the rich resources there. We must show them that Arathi will never again be a home for humans!\nGo to Arathi Basin and assault the mine, the lumber mill, the blacksmith and the stables. Pull down the enemies' banners, declaring those territories for the Horde.\nGo, ‹name›. Report back to me when this task is complete.","rew":"Money: 1 65 1 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+200 reputation with The Defilers","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.3,"y":29.7,"n":"Deathmaster Dwire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"680":{"id":680,"t":"The Real Threat","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Witchdoctor's Dress.","obj":"Slay Or'Kalar and bring his Head to Korin Fel in the Hammerfall outpost.\nOr'Kalar's Head Or'Kalar","desc":"You serve my husband well, ‹class›, but he does not know why Hammerfall is under attack.\nOr'Kalar, Mug'thol's pawn in Stromgarde, has an intense hatred for my husband, and wishes nothing more than my husband's death for defeating him years ago.\nMy auguries tell me that Or'Kalar has laid a trap for my husband, so I have hidden signs of the ogre's presence from him.\nMy husband will rush off foolishly if he learns of the ogre's whereabouts and I would ask for your help in slaying the creature.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMistspray Kilt Sword of Hammerfall Witchdoctor's Dress\nNew in Forever: Witchdoctor's Dress.\nExperience: 3,900\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Near the Tower of Arathor--that is where you will find Or'Kalar. His death will stop the attacks on Hammerfall and protect my husband's life.\nI see in your eyes that you think me weak--even dishonorable--for my silence. Some day you will learn what it is to love as I do. Perhaps then you will understand a different kind of strength and honor.\nIn the meantime, do as I ask, and slay Or'Kalar.","done":"You have done me a great service, ‹name›. Know that my husband's life and the safety of Hammerfall has been protected for another day because of your deeds. Please take this as a reward for your courage.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74,"y":33.1,"n":"Korin Fel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"5160":{"id":5160,"t":"The Matron Protectorate","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Winterspring and find Haleh. Give her Awbee's scale.\nAwbee's Scale\nProvided: Awbee's Scale","desc":"Travel to Kalimdor, ‹race›. Our flight makes its home in the frigid landscape of Winterspring. Once you reach Winterspring, find the caves of Mazthoril.\nUpon the icy floors of Mazthoril you will find cobalt runes. Hold one of my scales and stand upon a rune and you shall be transported to Haleh, our matron protectorate.\nGive her the scale so that she may scry what it is I have seen and felt, here in this doomed place.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"It is good to see you, ‹name›.","done":"The Aspects insist that we stay out of the affairs of mortals. In this world, however, such a thing is not always possible - especially when one of our own contemptuously disregards such edicts.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":54.5,"y":51.2,"n":"Haleh","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"2760":{"id":2760,"t":"The Mithril Order","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Galvan the Ancient in Stranglethorn Vale.\nMithril Pendant\nProvided: Mithril Pendant","desc":"Most of our recruits never make it to Booty Bay, ‹name›. The shine of the insignia is enough to trigger the loot lust in even the staunchest of blacksmiths. Fools they be, as the insignia is a drop in the bucket compared to the wealth of items you'll see!\nFind Galvan the Ancient and show him this pin. His residence is far to the north, between Zul Gurub and the Mosh'Ogg ogre mound.","rew":"Experience: 3,150","back":"Hail! Come closer; show Galvan what you have.","done":"Ah, many years it has been since one has been worthy of the mithril order's initiation. We will start now!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.9,"y":75.4,"n":"McGavan","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":50.6,"y":20.5,"n":"Galvan the Ancient","e":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97960":{"id":97960,"t":"Camping 101 skinning","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Rand Rhobart on the road to Undercity from Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your skinning skill to 20","desc":"Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.6,"y":60,"n":"Rand Rhobart","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94280":{"id":94280,"t":"Craftsmans writ mechanical dragonling","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Mechanical Dragonling\nMechanical Dragonling","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Mechanical Dragonling, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Mechanical Dragonling Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94280","cats":["crafting"]},"94360":{"id":94360,"t":"Craftsmans writ soul pouch","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Soul Pouch\nSoul Pouch","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Soul Pouch, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Soul Pouch Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94360","cats":["crafting"]},"2520":{"id":2520,"t":"Sathrah's Sacrifice","lv":12,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Priestess A'moora wants you to place Lady Sathrah's silvery spinnerets at the fountain inside the temple, and then return to her.\nProvided: Sathrah's Sacrifice","desc":"Now you must finish the task to which you have been appointed. Take the spinnerets and offer Lady Sathrah's sacrifice to Elune; lay the great spider to rest.\nInside this temple, find the central fountain. There is where you may leave the sacrifice. The holy waters will purify and cleanse the corruption that drove Sathrah mad.\nWhen you have completed this, return to me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLace Pants Cushioned Boots\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you placed the sacrifice at the fountain, ‹name›?","done":"The loss of Lady Sathrah is distressing, but in this way only may she be reborn with a renewed spirit.\nMay Elune willingly accept the sacrifice that you have offered her.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":36.7,"y":85.9,"n":"Priestess A'moora","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"7800":{"id":7800,"t":"A Donation of Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›, you've been a tremendous contributor to our cloth drive. As we work hard to replenish our reserves, one form of cloth remains critically low - runecloth. We are in absolutely dire need of runecloth, and we hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past.\nIf you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. We'll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we'll go from there.","done":"Fantastic - these will go right to use, I assure you. Thank you again for your assistance! We'd certainly be lost without you.\nWith all the donations you've made, I would certainly process any additional runecloth donations you care to make in the future. Just be sure to check in with me, and I'll personally make sure that your good deeds won't go unrecognized!","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":64,"y":23,"n":"Raedon Duskstriker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"1480":{"id":1480,"t":"The Corrupter","lv":33,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Flayed Demon Skin to Maurin Bonesplitter in Desolace.\nFlayed Demon Skin Burning Blade Seer 5 % , Burning Blade Invoker 5 % , Burning Blade Summoner 5 % , Burning Blade Shadowmage 5 % and 4 more\nProvided: Flayed Demon Skin","desc":"The torn skin smells rotten, and is remarkably pliable for something that appears to be dry and fragile.\nAs you unroll it, you can clearly see the red markings of some kind of language on one side. At the bottom of the skin is a very clear symbol that you guess is a signature of some kind.\nPerhaps it is something Maurin could tell you more about?","rew":"Experience: 1,300\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"The Burning Blade begin to realize how weak they truly are. Their magics are pathetic, their strength feeble.\nTheir only power comes from those they serve, and not from any understanding of true power and knowledge.","done":"Hmm, these runes are indeed a language, ‹name›, an old language. They seem remotely similar to the Eredun language, but the differences are drastic. If I am not mistaken, this is a contract of some kind.... Here, yes, this symbol is the demon's signature: Lord Azrethoc.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":52.2,"y":53.4,"n":"Maurin Bonesplitter","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"99160":{"id":99160,"t":"Rimes wrath","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Destroy 10 minor ice elementals.\nMinor Ice Elemental slain : 0/ 10","desc":"You may have noticed the elementals nearby. A shelf of rock and ice fell from the mountain peaks a few days ago and riled them up.\nThese frozen mountains are already treacherous for the average dwarf or human without the elements taking form. I am not one for fighting anymore--so any of the spirits you can kill would help make the road safer.","done":"I wish we could have simply placated them. Unfortunately it was beyond my knowledge and they were too dangerous to leave unchecked.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Father Gavin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"840":{"id":840,"t":"Conscript of the Horde","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Follow the western road from Razor Hill to the Barrens over a bridge.\nStop at the orc outpost across the bridge.\nGive Kargal Battlescar at the Barrens outpost your recruitment letter.\nRecruitment Letter\nProvided: Recruitment Letter","desc":"Hmm, you look pretty strong.\nListen, my good friend Kargal needs some new recruits for Barrens duty. I know you want to do what's right for the Horde. Well, this is your chance.\nTake this recruitment letter to Kargal and see if he'll sign it.","rew":"Experience: 460\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"What do you want, pup? If you're not here for recruitment, I don't have time for you.","done":"Oh, so Takrin sent you? He's an excellent scout, I'm not sure what I'd do without him.\nI'll sign your recruitment letter, but what we really need is someone at the Crossroads.\nDurotar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":50.8,"y":43.6,"n":"Takrin Pathseeker","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":19.4,"n":"Kargal Battlescar","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"1320":{"id":1320,"t":"The Black Shield","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.","desc":"Ah, I almost missed this... The leather strap on the back must have burned off, but it seems like it was made to fit a large person. I'd guess a tauren, actually.\nThat's about all I can tell you. Tell Captain Vimes I'm sorry I couldn't be of more help.","rew":"Experience: 1,350","done":"That's not much information to work on, but we'll have to keep it in mind. Hopefully some of the other pieces of this mystery will fall into place, and paint a more helpful picture of what happened.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":64.8,"y":50.4,"n":"Caz Twosprocket","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"1240":{"id":1240,"t":"The Troll Witchdoctor","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Defiant Orc Head to Kin'weelay in the Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.\nDefiant Orc Head\nProvided: Defiant Orc Head","desc":"We must know the events surrounding Marg's death! And the only way to do that, ‹name›, is through the witch-magic of trolls.\nBring Marg's head to Kin'weelay in Stranglethorn Vale, at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\nKin'weelay is the most powerful witchdoctor of the Darkspear trolls. If anyone can speak to Marg Nighteye's spirit, it is he.","rew":"Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"There is an angry spirit about you, brother/sister. What brings you to Kin'weelay?","done":"Ah, I now see. The spirit of this orc is bound in our world, boiling with rage from a task yet undone.\nWell, let us have words with this angry orc...\nDustwallow Marsh Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":35.2,"y":30.7,"n":"Nazeer Bloodpike","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.3,"y":27.7,"n":"Kin'weelay","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"40":{"id":40,"t":"A Fishy Peril","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Remy \"Two Times\" wants you to speak with Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.","desc":"‹name›, there's a new threat in Elwynn Forest! Murlocs are swimming up the streams of eastern Elwynn, scaring away fish and attacking gentle folk!\nI warned Marshal Dughan, but he's more worried about the gnolls and the bandits. He's not convinced that the murlocs are a danger.\nPlease, ‹name›, speak to Dughan and persuade him to send more troops to the east!","rew":"Experience: 85\n+10 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Yes, I spoke with Remy. I respect him as a merchant, though all reports of Murlocs to the east have been sketchy at best.\nYour concerns are noted, but unless I receive a military report of a murloc threat, we can't afford to send more troops east.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":67.3,"n":"Remy \"Two Times\"","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3640":{"id":3640,"t":"The Pledge of Secrecy","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you agree to become a Gnome Engineer, then right-click on the Pledge of Secrecy and speak once more with Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge.\nOverspark's Signed Pledge\nProvided: Overspark's Pledge of Secrecy","desc":"Gnome engineering is about engineering theory shaped to serve our needs! Our schemata allow us to make devices that control the world around us; the manual you read covered this.\nThe manual also covered our ages old oath of secrecy on our schemata. Once you become a gnome engineer, that's that. There is no access to goblin engineering at all.\nIf you still want to become a gnome engineer, sign this document pledging life-long secrecy and speak with me again. Think about it carefully, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"If you've signed the document and are ready to hand it to me, then that is that.\nThe secrets I will share with you are of such a magnitude that the signing of the Pledge of Secrecy is absolutely critical. I signed one, as did my brother and sister gnome engineers. You will be joining quite the auspicious fold, Engineer ‹name›!","done":"Welcome aboard, ‹name›! You soon will have access to the most advanced engineering schemata anywhere on Azeroth.\nNow that you have committed yourself to the pursuit of this knowledge, it is time to examine your gnome-oriented engineering work. From there, we'll help you build a plan to maximize your gnome engineering talents!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Tinkmaster Overspark","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"4120":{"id":4120,"t":"The Strength of Corruption","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache in Feralas wants you to kill 12 Angerclaw Grizzlies and 12 Felpaw Ravagers in Felwood.\nAngerclaw Grizzly slain : 0/ 12\nFelpaw Ravager slain : 0/ 12","desc":"Being a hunter, I strive to emulate the strengths I see in my opponents. It is possible to turn the battle in your favor by simply knowing your enemy well, ‹name›.\nIn a place called Felwood, north of Ashenvale, the creatures have been tainted by a substance called fel. The bears and wolves have been driven mad by it, but I believe that they have also grown even stronger as well.\nGo, ‹name›. Travel to Felwood and face these beasts. Learn for yourself if they are truly as strong as I believe.","rew":"Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Everything touched by the fel emanates a strange green glow... I sense it is evil, but at the same time, very powerful.","done":"It sounds from your descriptions as if the creatures show a mindless ferocity...\nStay alert, ‹name›. It would be in your best interest to learn more of the corruption. Always know your enemy.\nFeralas Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":76.2,"y":43.8,"n":"Talo Thornhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"520":{"id":520,"t":"The Crown of Will","lv":43,"min":34,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Mug'Thol, and return his head with the Crown of Will to Melisara in Tarren Mill.\nMug'thol's Head Mug'thol\nCrown of Will Mug'thol","desc":"With Mug'Thol's lieutenants dead, all that remains is to kill Mug'Thol and retrieve the Crown of Will. I have no doubt he'll be reluctant to part with it. Most likely expecting you, too, given the... departure... of his fellows.\nFind Mug'Thol, and deliver his head and the Crown to me. The Crushridge resistance will be at an end.","rew":"Experience: 4,450\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Three heads I have, a fourth I need. It will be Mug'Thol's, or it will be yours, ‹name›. That I promise.","done":"You have done your duty well, ‹name›. Mug'Thol's head shall adorn the highest peak of the ruins of Alterac, and the Deathguard will sweep the remnants of the Crushridge into the ground.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.6,"y":20.6,"n":"Melisara","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"9320":{"id":9320,"t":"Major Mana Potion","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 50 instead of 55.","obj":"15 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nMajor Mana Potion","back":"In addition to our other supplies, we also have a number of major mana potions you may find useful. I will give you one in exchange for fifteen necrotic runes.","done":"Here you are, ‹name›. Be careful out there. Our numbers are not so large we can afford many battlefield casualties.\nUndercity Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":65,"y":45.6,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.2,"y":73.8,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":42.1,"y":58.5,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"9000":{"id":9000,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Deliana your Beaststalker's Cap and Beaststalker's Tunic.\nBeaststalker's Cap Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nBeaststalker's Tunic General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"That's an amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved. Now maybe I'll be able to sleep at night with both eyes shut.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you'll really enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nBeastmaster's Cap Beastmaster's Tunic\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Beaststalker pieces in exchange for your new Beastmaster's Cap and Tunic?","done":"I'm going to miss you, ‹name›. I owe you such a debt of gratitude; I think I'll never be able to repay it.\nI hope that you enjoy your new head and chest armor, and that it protects you for a long time to come.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"280":{"id":280,"t":"A Dark Threat Looms","lv":18,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Chief Engineer Hinderweir wants you to swim down to the base of the dam, locate the powder keg and stir in the Disarming Mixture to prevent an explosion.\nDisarming Mixture\nProvided: Disarming Mixture","desc":"Earlier today I spotted some Dark Iron Insurgents swimming toward the Dam with a large keg. No Mountaineers were on hand to stop them! I'm afraid they've planted the Seaforium at the base of the Dam and it could blow at any minute! Let me combine all these ingredients into the Disarming Mixture. There we go.\nNow I need you to take this mixture and stir it into the keg before it's too late! Hurry!","rew":"Experience: 675\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"The top of the keg slowly twists off.","done":"The keg fizzles slightly as the Disarming Mixture settles in.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":46,"y":13.6,"n":"Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":50.6,"y":14.3,"n":"Explosive Charge","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8680":{"id":8680,"t":"Windtotem the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.7,"n":"Elder Windtotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1880":{"id":1880,"t":"Mage-tastic Gizmonitor","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Bink her Mage-tastic Gizmonitor.\nMage-tastic Gizmonitor Bink's Toolbox","desc":"We mages do more than just waggle our fingers and make pretty sparks! We control magic, the base fabric of our world! And that takes great care, and resolve. And knowledge... so much knowledge!\nOne of my devices, the mage-tastic gizmonitor, collects and stores that knowledge in huge amounts! But it's lost! When we fled our home of Gnomeregan, I left it in a chest in one of our huts outside the city, and now the place is crawling with leper gnomes!\nPlease, ‹name›, retrieve my gizmonitor!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nArcane Orb Arcane Staff\nExperience: 850","back":"Did you find the gizmonitor? I must have it before its energy supply runs out!","done":"Oh, splendid day! When I made the gizmonitor I never realized how dependent on it I would become. Now I can begin my studies anew!\nThank you, ‹name›! And here--these were my first tools as a mage. They're a little scratched but they're well tested. Take your pick--I'm sure you'll find either of them useful.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":22.4,"n":"Bink","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"1960":{"id":1960,"t":"Investigate the Alchemist Shop","lv":16,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Obtain a Cantation of Manifestation and a Chest of Containment Coffers from behind Anastasia Hartwell. Bring 3 Filled Containment Coffers, the Chest of Containment Coffers and the Cantation of Manifestation to Anastasia in the Undercity.\n3 Filled Containment Coffer Filled Containment Coffer\nChest of Containment Coffers Chest of Containment Coffers\nCantation of Manifestation Cantation of Manifestation","desc":"Algernon's alchemist shop in the Apothecarium is the locus of a strange disturbance. Invisible creatures, made solely of magic, wander the shop--there must be a reason, and we must find it!\nInvestigate the disturbance and capture those creatures. Take a chest of coffers and a scroll from behind me. Use the scroll at the shop to make the creatures visible, subdue them with your spells, then throw down a coffer to capture them. Return with the filled coffers, the empty coffers and the cantation.","rew":"Experience: 1,150","back":"Have you investigated the disturbance, ‹name›? Have you captured the creatures?","done":"Very good, ‹name›. The creatures within these containment coffers will be studied by our finest minds, and the reason behind their presence in the Undercity will be determined.\nIf their appearance is caused by a rift in the natural flow of magic, then we must determine if the rift was random. If it was not random, but instead an attack by some magical force, then we must prepare for future, more serious disturbances.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":10,"n":"Anastasia Hartwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"99080":{"id":99080,"t":"Drive them out","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 6 Galak Centaurs, 4 Galak Outrunners, and bring the head of Herak the Pillager to Baine Bloodhoof.\nGalak Centaur slain : 0/ 6\nGalak Outrunner slain : 0/ 4\nHerak's Head","desc":"Hear my words well: we will not yield a single blade of grass to the centaur.\nGo to their camp now, before they have rested and have a chance to ride to our village. Slaughter them all. Ensure none escape to the Barrens to rally others to their aid.\nIf you find the leader of this would-be raiding party, bring me his head so that it may serve as a warning to others who dare tread on our ancestral homeland.","back":"Is the deed done?","done":"You are covered in centaur blood. Remember this feeling. It is an honor unlike any other among our people.\nI could hear the moment the last fell, and their thunderous stampede echoed no longer. Well done!\nToday marks a great victory for our village, and a security our young ones need now more than ever. You have my deepest thanks, young ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.4,"y":60.2,"n":"Baine Bloodhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"760":{"id":760,"t":"Wildmane Cleansing","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Wildmane Cleansing Totem at the Wildmane Water Well, then return to Mull Thunderhorn.\nProvided: Wildmane Cleansing Totem","desc":"Your cleansing of the Winterhoof and Thunderhorn wells is spoken among the spirits, young ‹name›. The Wildmane Totem is made, and your last task lies ahead.\nThe Wildmane Water Well lies north of Thunder Bluff. Perform the ritual! Heal the land of the goblins' poisons! Let clean water flow once again!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCeremonial Tomahawk Dreamwatcher Staff\nExperience: 1,050\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The last water well remains fetid and poisonous, ‹name›. You must not delay!","done":"You've done it. You have cleaned the wells, and healed our land. Bloodhoof village is grateful, ‹name›.\nMay the wind whisper your deeds for a hundred seasons, and may the waters of Mulgore remain clean forever.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.5,"y":63.6,"n":"Mull Thunderhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9080":{"id":9080,"t":"Bonescythe Pauldrons","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -50g instead of 0.","obj":"Rohan the Assassin at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Bonescythe Pauldrons if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Pauldrons, 12 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 5 Cured Rugged Hides, 1 Nexus Crystal and 50 gold pieces.\nDesecrated Pauldrons Grobbulus 0 % in Naxxramas , Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Patchwerk 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n5 Cured Rugged Hide\nNexus Crystal","desc":"If you want Bonescythe made, you're going to have to supply the materials.\nEnter Naxxramas, the big floating city of death in the sky up there, and find desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps. Bring those back along with the materials to put everything together and you'll have your Bonescythe. Oh, and you'll need to pay me for my troubles... I'll supply the bones.","rew":"You will receive:\nBonescythe Pauldrons\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"<Rohan eyes you suspiciously.>\nBeen to Tyr's Hand lately?","done":"<Rohan wipes the sweat from his brow.>\nThese shoulders took some work! Don't go out and get yourself killed like a scrub, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.9,"n":"Rohan the Assassin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9240":{"id":9240,"t":"Glacial Vest","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -300g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 8 Frozen Runes, 8 Bolts of Runecloth, 6 Essences of Water, 4 Ironweb Spider Silks and 300 gold. You must also be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.\n8 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n8 Bolt of Runecloth Felsteel Chest 0.9 % , Twilight Lord Everun 0 %\n6 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n4 Ironweb Spider Silk Mother Smolderweb 50 % , Crystal Fang 47 % , Gretheer 16.2 % , Plague Lurker 13.9 % and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion, may he rest in peace, I am now able to create a Glacial vest. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nGlacial Vest","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8920":{"id":8920,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Bracers of Valor to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\n15 Silithus Venom Sample Stonelash Scorpid 30 % , Stonelash Pincer 30 % , Stonelash Flayer 30 % , Sand Skitterer 30 % and 1 more\nBracers of Valor Blackhand Iron Guard 6.7 % , Smolderthorn Axe Thrower 4.5 % , Firebrand Legionnaire 3.5 % , Bloodaxe Warmonger 2.4 % and 2 more","desc":"Hail, ‹class›! I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world. Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.\nPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.\nI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus. Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","rew":"You will receive:\nBracers of Heroism\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you obtained the items I require, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes. Mux will be quite happy with this.\nThose bracers were part of a larger armor set. If you're interested in providing me with further assistance, I'd be willing to consider parting with the rest of it.\nOrgrimmar Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"94440":{"id":94440,"t":"A lesson in divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Retrieve the Scarlet Crusade Attack Plans from the Scarlet Crusaders at Venomweb Vale, and return to Deathguard Billmuth at Tyr's Watch.\nScarlet Crusade Attack Plans","desc":"These Scarlet Crusaders often carry satchels with their deployment orders. We know an attack is coming, but if we can recover their orders, we can warn the rest of the Deathguard and prepare an ambush.\nYou are clearly an impressive paladin. Kill these scarlet animals and retrieve a copy of their orders and bring them back to Deathguard Billmuth. He'll take it from there.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 675","back":"What news of Deathguard Falgan?","done":"Thank you for saving my friend,Mortikkar. I will take these plans back to my commander and we will give those crusaders a welcoming they won't forget.\nI know that many among our people mistrust you paladins, but its clear to me that you are Forsaken through and through. I won't forget this, and I'll make sure others know of what you did here today.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":86.6,"y":47.6,"n":"Deathguard Falgan","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Deathguard Billmuth","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"3000":{"id":3000,"t":"Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.","desc":"Hello, ‹name›. I know you're busy helping out the people of Azeroth, but when you have the time, you should return to Ironforge and speak to one of the most respected paladins of your home: Tiza Battleforge. She's the one the younger dwarven paladins go to when it is time they learn more about the Light and what's expected of all of us.\nYou can find her upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries which is located in the Mystic Ward.","rew":"Experience: 230","done":"I greet you, and bid you welcome, ‹name›.\nStormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":23,"n":"Tiza Battleforge","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7640":{"id":7640,"t":"Exorcising Terrordale","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Exorcism Censer to drive out the spirits that torment Terrordale. When you have slain 25 Terrordale Spirits, return to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind.\nExorcism Censer\nTerrordale Spirit slain : 0/ 25\nProvided: Exorcism Censer","desc":"I have added a pinch of dirt from the tainted ground of Terrordale in the Eastern Plaguelands to the censer. You will now use this censer to find areas there that show signs of spiritual turmoil and disturbance. Look for green auras that permeate the ground as the physical world buckles under the torment of the spirit realm and use the censer to drive out the evil spirits.\nWhen you have passed sufficient judgment on the spirits there, you will be ready to proceed.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"It is good to see you again ‹name›. Is your work done in Terrordale?","done":"Well done, ‹name›. To render the judgment of the Light on those that dwell in darkness is a task we must approach with vim and zeal; you have done just that with your sacrifice in Ironforge and your judgments of the spirits in Terrordale.\nYour next steps will call on both sacrifice and judgment again as you now strive to reclaim the spirit of a fallen charger who now serves a Death Knight known as Darkreaver.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5640":{"id":5640,"t":"Desperate prayer","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, ‹name›.\nAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.\nWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out one of your High Priestesses for further training.","done":"I'm glad you've arrived, ‹name›. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.\nThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we'll begin discussing some of those now.\nDarnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.2,"y":81,"n":"Priestess Alathea","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.8,"y":26.4,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"120":{"id":120,"t":"Messenger to Stormwind","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Magistrate Solomon has given you a report which must be delivered to General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind. The judge wants you to return to him as soon as the delivery has been made.\nThe State of Lakeshire\nProvided: The State of Lakeshire","desc":"These are trying times, ‹class›. The township is under constant siege. Without reinforcements, we will certainly face defeat. The message I now entrust to you is of utmost importance. Get this report to General Marcus Jonathan of Stormwind immediately. Once your delivery is made, return to me at once with any news, be it good or bad.\nNow make haste!","rew":"Experience: 490\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What have you there?","done":"At ease, ‹class›.\nMagistrate Solomon is a noble leader. His words carry great weight with me. I shall seek the counsel of the King and make the situation clear to him. Assure the good judge that he has the Stormwind Army's support. Reinforcements will be sent as soon as word is given from His Majesty.\nRedridge Mountains Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":69.2,"y":82.7,"n":"General Marcus Jonathan","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8840":{"id":8840,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horde Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Orgrimmar.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":61.9,"y":45.3,"n":"Officer Gothena","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"2360":{"id":2360,"t":"Mathias and the Defias","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Westfall and find Agent Kearnen for your debriefing.","desc":"Not a moment too soon, ‹name›. SI:7 reconnaissance is reporting unusually heavy Defias activity in Westfall.\nIt would seem that the Defias have taken over an abandoned Alliance watch tower southeast of Sentinel Hill and are using it as a base of operations to smuggle in goods from the Redridge supply route.\nGet to Westfall and contact Agent Kearnen for your debriefing. You will find her hidden near the tower.\n...and ‹name›, should you be discovered, SI:7 will disavow all knowledge of your existence.","rew":"Experience: 390","done":"Mathias finally sent another agent to back me up, eh? Well I hope he's ready to hear some bad news.\nStormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":68.5,"y":70.1,"n":"Agent Kearnen","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1160":{"id":1160,"t":"Test of Lore","lv":36,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,000 experience instead of 2,100, 2.38 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Find The Beginnings of the Undead Threat, and return it to Parqual Fintallas in Undercity.\nBeginnings of the Undead Threat Beginnings of the Undead Threat in Scarlet Monastery","desc":"I will tell you what you must seek, and I will even ask you my question, but not because you wish to prove yourself. Knowledge is far more important than strength. Even as others seem to pass you by in ability, your knowledge of the world will be more valuable.\nGo to the Monastery in the north of Tirisfal Glades. In the library there, a book called Beginnings of the Undead Threat resides. It was used by the now-corrupt paladins there to train them to fight my kind.\nBring it to me.","rew":"Experience: 5,000\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"I hope you made the Scarlet Crusade suffer some before stealing the book from them.\nMy views of their kind are not unwarranted. The Crusade may have been followers of the Light at one time, but now, they seek to destroy any creatures that have not sided with their religion. They believe all undead, Forsaken or otherwise, must be cleansed, and those traveling in their lands must either be insane, or subject to the undead's powerful magics. Idiots. Idiots and fools; all of them.","done":"This is the book I sent you to search for.\n<Parqual slowly caresses his hand over the top of the book as he stares down at it.>\nSo now you wish a question to prove your mind is as powerful as your body and spirit. If you have studied the book long enough, then I shall ask you your question and you can be done with these tests!","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":57.8,"y":65.4,"n":"Parqual Fintallas","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scarlet-monastery"]},"8360":{"id":8360,"t":"Dancing for Marzipan","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Do a dance emote at Innkeeper Pala, and in exchange you'll receive Thunder Bluff Marzipan!","desc":"Even though you're trick-or-treating for a sick child, you still need to perform a trick for the treat! We can't very well change the tradition, now can we...\nI believe the cost of a piece of marzipan nowadays is to bust out and DANCE! That's right, let me see your moves! Dance for me, and I'll give you some tasty marzipan!","rew":"You will receive:\nThunder Bluff Marzipan","back":"You know how to dance, don't you? Try by putting your right foot in... then your right foot out... your right foot in... shake it all about...","done":"You're quite the dancing machine, ‹name›!\nHere's your treat for being such a good sport. Happy Hallow's End, and give my best to your sick little friend! I hope they get better soon.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":45.8,"y":64.7,"n":"Innkeeper Pala","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8280":{"id":8280,"t":"Securing the Supply Lines","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to kill 15 Dredge Strikers.\nDredge Striker slain : 0/ 15","desc":"Cenarion Hold is a location of utmost strategic importance. I'm convinced that while we hold it our victory over the silithid is guaranteed. Provided our influx supplies can be maintained, that is.\nDesert worms have proven to be more of a threat to our supply caravans than even the silithid themselves. Just this morning, a large shipment of morrowgrain was ravaged by a group of dredge strikers. I need you to thin their numbers to ensure our supplies aren't jeopardized.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"The dredge strikers are a serious threat and must be dealt with quickly!","done":"You have my sincere gratitude. Your efforts in helping Cenarion Hold have shown true courage.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"440":{"id":440,"t":"The Engraved Ring","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Deliah's Ring to Magistrate Sevren in Brill.\nDeliah's Ring\nProvided: Deliah's Ring","desc":"If you want to find the husband or beloved who gave Deliah her ring... then speak with Magistrate Sevren in Brill. He should have records of recent deaths and, with luck, can discover who Deliah is.\nBut I wouldn't hope. Whoever gave her the ring is probably dead. Or if he's undead he probably no longer cares about Deliah.","rew":"Experience: 575\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Hello, ‹name›. What brings you back to Brill?","done":"A Deliah did live in Brill not long ago. She was buried in the mass grave but if what you say is true, then the Rot Hide Gnolls must have stolen her body and taken it to Silverpine.\nThe Rot Hides, like all the Scourge, must be destroyed. I trust you are taking steps to make that happen.\nSilverpine Forest Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.3,"y":50.8,"n":"Magistrate Sevren","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1800":{"id":1800,"t":"Lordaeron Throne Room","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take your ward to the old Lordaeron Throne Room that lies just before descending into the Undercity.","desc":"The orphan matrons at my home tell mighty stories of battle and lore at night if we are good and do our chores. One story was about how Lordaeron fell, and about how the evil Arthas took his own father's life to become ruler.\nHe had no honor, ‹name›! When I grow up and become a mighty Horde warrior, my blade will be guided by honor - never evil!\nWould you take me to see the throne room, please? It is just before where you would go down into the Undercity.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Horde","back":"Are we there yet?","done":"That throne room was scary, ‹name›! Even though it was empty, it felt like a great evil had happened there. I felt mad... but I also felt sad too. I understand why the matrons tell us such stories; I will never betray my people like that!\nThank you for taking me to the throne room, ‹name›. I learned a lot.\nTirisfal Glades Open the zone on the world map Start Orcish Orphan End Orcish Orphan Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Horde Shareable No Quest ID 1800\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 650 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Children's Week\nUse the Orcish Orphan Whistle to talk with the child you will be looking after during Children's Week.\nOrphan Matron Battlewail Orgrimmar\n2 [ 60 ] Lordaeron Throne Room this quest\nTake your ward to the old Lordaeron Throne Room that lies just before descending into the Undercity.\nOrcish Orphan\n650 XP","cats":["special"]},"1080":{"id":1080,"t":"Covert Ops - Beta","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Venture Co. Letters from Windshear Mine at the east end of Windshear Crag.\nVenture Co. Letters Venture Co. Documents\nProvided: Covert Ops Pack","desc":"Plan Beta's just like Plan Alpha, ‹name›.\nWe cause a distraction and then steal their precious letters.\nThe key is to get their letters... remember that.\nThe pages I gave you already will tell you where to plant the explosives. Just get back here alive and with those letters....","rew":"Experience: 2,200\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"How'd it go, ‹name›?","done":"Incredible, ‹name›! Kaela and the Sentinels will be so happy. With your skill and my creations, we're unstoppable.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.5,"y":67.1,"n":"Gaxim Rustfizzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"200":{"id":200,"t":"Bookie Herod","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Bookie Herod's Records.","desc":"If Kurzen knows Thorsen's secret, then we have a spy in our midst. We must determine how the secret was leaked!\nThorsen's contact within Kurzen's camp was Bookie Herod. Herod is Kurzen's logistics officer and knows everything about the running of Kurzen's Compound. If you can get Herod's notes or records, maybe we can find out how Thorsen was discovered.\nWhen we were still with Kurzen, Bookie's office was on the top floor of the camp's only two-story house. His records are probably still there.","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","done":"These are Bookie Herod's notes and records.\nAmong them are: a list of supplies within the camp, material requests from Colonel Kurzen, and various letters and correspondences.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3,"n":"Lieutenant Doren","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":43.7,"y":9.4,"n":"Bookie Herod's Records","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"600":{"id":600,"t":"Venture Company Mining","lv":41,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Singing Blue Crystals to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay.\n10 Singing Blue Crystal Foreman Cozzle 80 % , Venture Co. Tinkerer 80 % , Venture Co. Surveyor 80 % , Venture Co. Foreman 80 % and 2 more","desc":"The Venture Company has a string of operations through Stranglethorn which keeps hard-working goblins, like me, from making honest gold! Please, you must help me!\nThe Venture Company is mining near the Crystalvein Mine to the north. They can't get into the mine because of all the basilisks, but they're still able to dig up Singing Crystals from the surrounding hills.\nTake their crystals from them, and show them they don't have the run of the jungle.\nAnd... um... bring me those crystals as proof!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGoblin Igniter Silver Spade\nExperience: 3,300\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Do you have those crystals?? I need them!!\nI mean...I need to know the evil Venture Company is losing ground in Stranglethorn. Because, you know, we honest folk have to make a living!","done":"Great! Wonderful! I can get a bundle for these!!\nThat Venture Company sure picked the wrong jungle to mine in, didn't they? We'd all be in better shape if they moved out of here.\nThank you, ‹name›. You've done a good deed this day.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.1,"y":77.2,"n":"Crank Fizzlebub","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1560":{"id":1560,"t":"Tooga's Quest","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Show Tooga the way back to his wife, Torta.","desc":"I am so lost!\nMy wife, Torta, sent me out to fetch dinner and I must have taken a wrong turn somewhere.\nWould you be so kind as to lead me back to Torta? She's waiting for me just south of Steamwheedle Port.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nChelonian Cuffs Band of the Great Tortoise\nExperience: 5,900","back":"Where is Tooga?","done":"So he couldn't find his way back on his own? Figures.\nWell, I guess you deserve something for your troubles....","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":31.8,"y":74.1,"n":"Tooga","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":66.6,"y":25.7,"n":"Torta","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8760":{"id":8760,"t":"The Path of the Invoker","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Dedication of this magnitude is a rarity. You have shown that your will is unfaltering, ‹name›. You shall be greatly rewarded for your stalwart watch over our world.\nHand me your signet ring so that I may strengthen its enchantment.","done":"Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, ‹name›. May you never stray from the path of the invoker!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"920":{"id":920,"t":"Tenaron's Summons","lv":5,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tenaron Stormgrip atop Aldrassil in Shadowglen.","desc":"‹name›, is it? I heard that Tenaron has been asking for you. You'll find him in the highest room atop Aldrassil.\nWe may live long lives, but it's best you not keep him waiting too long.","rew":"Experience: 45\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Ah, ‹name›. I was hoping you'd be prompt in answering my summons. I have an important task that I would like you to perform.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.8,"y":41.7,"n":"Gilshalan Windwalker","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":59.1,"y":39.4,"n":"Tenaron Stormgrip","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"2040":{"id":2040,"t":"Underground Assault","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,700 experience instead of 1,550, 2.39 times as much. New rewards: Bravo's Armbands, Dreamer's Leggings. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon que","obj":"Retrieve the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket from the Deadmines and return it to Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind.\nGnoam Sprecklesprocket Sneed's Shredder in The Deadmines","desc":"Gnomeregan has fallen under the control of those dastardly troggs! The situation is grave but perhaps you can help, ‹name›.\nDeep in the Deadmines is a functional goblin shredder. Find that shredder and bring back the intact power supply. With the shredder's power supply, we can give our gyrodrillmatic excavationators the power they need to break through the rocky underground borders of Gnomeregan, opening the way for a gnomish assault!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPolar Gauntlets Sable Wand Bravo's Armbands Dreamer's Leggings\nNew in Forever: Bravo's Armbands, Dreamer's Leggings.\nExperience: 3,700\n+100 reputation with Stormwind\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Have you found the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket, ‹name›?","done":"Well done, ‹name›. Thanks to you, Gnomeregan is one step closer to its day of liberation!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.6,"y":34.1,"n":"Shoni the Shilent","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-deadmines"]},"2440":{"id":2440,"t":"The Platinum Discs","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the reward voucher to Bena Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff.\nReward Voucher\nProvided: Reward Voucher","desc":"I shall focus my energies on these discs; they will reveal their true workings to me in due time.\nAs for you ‹name›, I will now reward you for your diligence in bringing this to my attention. Take this voucher to Bena Winterhoof, the alchemy trainer for Thunder Bluff. She will give you a special item I believe you will find appealing, and she will supply you with a choice of potions from my personal stock.\nReturn to me soon, as I sense there is much more at hand for us to do regarding this find.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Superior Healing Potion 5 Greater Mana Potion\nYou will also receive:\nThawpelt Sack\nExperience: 420\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Greetings, ‹class›! Are you here for alchemy training, or perhaps something else?","done":"Well ‹name›, you must have pleased Sage Truthseeker greatly for him to give you this item. You are also to be granted a gift from his cache of potions; you may choose between 5 superior healing potions or 5 greater mana potions as your reward.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":34.4,"y":46.9,"n":"Sage Truthseeker","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":46.6,"y":33.2,"n":"Bena Winterhoof","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"1000":{"id":1000,"t":"The New Frontier","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.","desc":"Attention, heroes!\nThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor! A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.\nAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle. Speak with the Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder's Rise of Thunder Bluff for more information!","rew":"Experience: 550\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Greetings, ‹class›.\nI am pleased to see the likes of you taking an interest in the well being of nature; tales of your mighty deeds precede you, and you are welcomed here. Seeing you before me instills the feeling of confidence that the Cenarion Circle will get the proper aid it needs.\nOur connection with the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade transcends racial and political divides. Remember this as you work on behalf of the Circle, and you will do well.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":44.3,"y":58.8,"n":"Bluff Runner Windstrider","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"360":{"id":360,"t":"Return to the Magistrate","lv":9,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Magistrate Sevren in Brill.","desc":"Now return to Magistrate Sevren with the information I gave you. He'll want it as soon as possible, so be swift.\nAnd if you see any Scourge on your way back, take them down - we can't let them wander our lands unchallenged.","rew":"Money: 1 50 0 gold, 1 silver, 50 copper Experience: 390\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"It is troubling to hear of the Scourge slipping past the Bulwark. The Lich King and his minions are ceaseless in their assaults.\nBut we will not give in. He will not take us again!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.5,"y":60.3,"n":"Deathguard Linnea","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.3,"y":50.8,"n":"Magistrate Sevren","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2200":{"id":2200,"t":"Back to Uldaman","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search for clues as to the current disposition of Talvash's necklace within Uldaman. The slain paladin he mentioned was the person who had it last.\nProvided: Talvash's Phial of Scrying","desc":"A competitor of mine started a rumor that my necklace cursed the paladin. Needless to say, no one wants to buy cursed items from a jeweler.\n‹name›, I'll make you a deal - find the gems and I'll reassemble the necklace, so long as you'll advertise that I do NOT make cursed items!\nTry looking for clues in Uldaman; maybe see if the paladin's body is down there, since he's the one who we know had it last! When you find the gems you should use this; it'll allow you to contact me here in Ironforge.","rew":"Experience: 2,550\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"Remains of a paladin: Reading the journal reveals that after much effort, the paladin had identified the location of all three missing gems:\nThe Shadowforge dwarves hid the ruby in their barricaded area as they battled the Troggs for control of Uldaman.\nThe troggs stashed the topaz in an urn located near some unusual inhabitants of Uldaman - Alliance dwarves!\nFinally, the trogg elder himself took the sapphire as his own.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.9,"y":21.7,"n":"Talvash del Kissel","s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"2280":{"id":2280,"t":"The Platinum Discs","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the miniature version of the Discs of Norgannon to the one of the sages in Thunder Bluff.\nMiniature Platinum Discs\nProvided: Miniature Platinum Discs","desc":"Touching the Discs of Norgannon once again makes your hand tingle. This time, however, a strange grinding noise is heard from inside the discs.\nYour backpack suddenly becomes heavier than it was before. Inside, you discover a miniature version of the discs!\nNo doubt, an item of this sort would be invaluable for someone interested in the ancient history of Azeroth. The sages of Thunder Bluff are such historians, known throughout the Horde; perhaps they can make good use of it.","rew":"Experience: 5,250\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Yes young one, I see you marching into my tent with intensity in your stride... with determination in your purpose. You seek my counsel is some matter of grave importance to the Horde? Perhaps you wish a mystery of the universe revealed to you?","done":"What are these here then?\nImpressive, young one! These discs, in them I sense secrets that the earth has held on to tightly for many years. You were very wise to bring them here to me.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":34.4,"y":46.9,"n":"Sage Truthseeker","e":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"1640":{"id":1640,"t":"Beat Bartleby","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Beat Bartleby, then talk to him.","desc":"You want what?? You're crazy!\nThe only way you'll get this mug is if you pry it from my cold, dead fingers...","rew":"Experience: 210","back":"The only way you'll get this mug is if you pry it from my cold, dead fingers...","done":"You're a lot tougher than you look!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":76.8,"y":52.5,"n":"Bartleby","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"92840":{"id":92840,"t":"Catching wind","lv":11,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take the Index Esoteria to the Overlook Standing Stones in Shen'dar Highlands and use it on the Windstone Formations in the area to gather data.\nGather Data on Elemental Currents : 0/ 6\nProvided: Index Esoteria","desc":"Fillion was sent to the Overlook Standing Stones with a special device used to measure and study the elemental energy there.\nTake this--an Index Esoteria--and use it to extract data from the massive windstone formations that form there. Be on your guard however, as the Windshapers are likely to be jealously guarding this site now.\nShould any attempt to obstruct you, well... do what you need to do. I have no more patience for their interference.","rew":"You will receive:\nBow of Hours 5 Minor Troll's Blood Elixir\nMoney: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 875\n+100 reputation with High Order","back":"It's often difficult for me to establish a distinction between the Windshapers and the Al'Aketh, save that one is more overtly violent than the other. Equally slavish to their misplaced beliefs, they are both equally dangerous if left to their own devices.\nThey see our desire to better understand this realm and its magic as a desecration of their traditions. Their small-mindedness is why our mission is so important. If not us, who will have the courage to save Zephras?","done":"It would not have been my preference to spill Windshaper blood but the blame for this pointless conflict rests solely on their shoulders. We sought to peacefully gather information, and they responded with violence.\nUnfortunately, word has spread and the Windshapers are already calling it a 'massacre'. They wouldn't dare to retaliate here in Valanaar, but they will certainly not forget.\n‹name›, you have been of tremendous aid to the High Order. Thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.6,"y":79.8,"n":"Elaadrin Evengale","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93320":{"id":93320,"t":"Tower defense","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report to Yorana Windyreed at the eastern watchtower in the Gustberry Lowlands.","desc":"I've just received word that the cult is attacking the pylon watchtower just outside of town! I've sent the few extra peacekeepers we have here to try and break through the enemy back line to relieve the defenders, but any additional help could mean the difference between our people there living or dying.\nPlease leave immediately for the east watchtower and provide whatever aid you can.\nMy lieutenant Yorana Windyreed led the relief force. If she still lives she can tell you how best to help.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDefender's Bracers Windswept Slippers Peacekeeper's Legguards\nExperience: 440\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","done":"We are holding them off for now, but they have greater numbers and our fighters are starting to get tired. We need to do something to break the stalemate, and do it fast.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":69.6,"y":67,"n":"Yorana Windyreed","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93160":{"id":93160,"t":"The forests bounty","lv":13,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 8 Shadowgale Acorns in Shadowgale Forest.\n8 Zephyrseed","desc":"I do appreciate you stopping by to talk with me! I-If you do want to help out, I could use a bit of help gathering up acorns from the forest floor. I've gathered most of the ones close by but there sure are a lot of raptor-bird things in the forest. It's dangerous out there and I'd rather not become a giant bird's lunch!\nSo if you want, you could maybe gather them for me? I'll make us something tasty if you do!","back":"Mmm, I think you are going to like what I can cook up with these acorns!","done":"Thank you, stranger! You'll find that these are delicious once roasted!\nPlease excuse me, it won't take me long to whip this up.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":54,"y":39,"n":"Strange Hermit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});